{
    /* Relaxation of Laplace's equation on a grid whose boundary is held at
       zero: every sweep replaces a cell by the mean of its four neighbours.

       The compiler proves the values stay within the range they started in,
       so the contract holds at every sweep. It does *not* prove convergence:
       the update's coefficients sum to exactly 1, and the ∞-norm argument the
       checker makes stops there. The iteration does converge — by a spectral
       argument this checker does not make — and the kernel reports whether it
       stopped on the tolerance or on the cap.

         rhoc examples/laplace.rho --tau 1e-6 --max-iter 2000
    */
    INPUT:◯ □ 32 32
    INPUT → U
    ((▷0U + ▽0U + ▷1U + ▽1U) / 4.0) ⇒ U
    U → =
}
